## Repository Structure (`tree -L 2 -a`, gitignored folders marked)

```
{{PROJECT_NAME}}/
├── {{MODULE_NAME}}/         # THE package, flat layout, named after the repo
│   ├── data/  models/  losses/  metrics/  train/  utils/     # mandatory subpackages
│   ├── scripts/             # CLIs: {{PROJECT_NAME}}-main.py, {{PROJECT_NAME}}-eval.py, dm_link.py
│   ├── slurm/               # cluster job scripts
│   ├── <domain>/ ...        # project-specific subpackages
│   └── __init__.py  __main__.py  app.py  py.typed
├── configs/                 # one yaml per experiment
├── notebooks/               # capabilities.ipynb: quick checks of what the repo can do
├── tests/                   # pytest
├── third_party/             # external repos as git submodules
├── .docs/                   # the record (hidden: needs `tree -a`)
│   ├── progress.md          #   timetable + log + todos — committed
│   ├── figures/  latex-draft/  runs/<run-name>/
├── resources/               # gitignored, built per machine by {{MODULE_NAME}}/scripts/dm_link.py
│   ├── data/                #   dataset links + generated/
│   └── pretrained-checkpoints/
├── outputs/                 # gitignored: one directory per run + background-job logs
│   ├── <experiment>-000/    #   config.json, metrics.jsonl, val_<step>.json, last.pt, best.pt, DONE
│   ├── <experiment>-<tag>/  #   short test runs, same layout
│   └── logs/                #   stdout of background jobs, slurm-*.out
├── config-global.json       # nas_root, machines, workspaces, datasets, checkpoints, methods, smoke
├── pyproject.toml  uv.lock  .python-version
├── README.md  HANDOFF.md  instructions.md
└── .gitignore  .gitmodules
```

### .docs/

`.docs/progress.md` is the single source of truth: a gantt timetable at the
top, a dated log in the middle, todos at the bottom — all three sharing the
same section names. Everything else in `.docs/` supports it.

`.docs/` is dot-prefixed and hidden by default in Obsidian and most file
browsers; enable "Show hidden files" to see it.

